  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Stephen Winchell said in August 2025 that finding vulnerabilities and patching codebases is slow, expensive, and dependent on a limited workforce, especially as adversaries use AI to amplify exploits. He also said AIxCC-developed technology would give defenders an edge in identifying and patching vulnerabilities at speed and scale. In an official-role statement, he said AIxCC exemplifies DARPA’s high-risk, high-reward programs and that releasing cyber reasoning systems open source makes the tools available to cyber defenders. A 2018 reported statement attributed to Winchell described a technology as high-risk but high-payoff and potentially leading to a decisive combat advantage.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s4",
    "s3"
   ],
